---
/* Concise road guide for the Shimla → Kinnaur → Spiti → Manali circuit. Facts are kept general and
   hedged; timings, openings and permits are always confirmed for the traveller's dates. */
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import WhatsAppLink from '../components/conversion/WhatsAppLink.astro';
import { buildPageMeta } from '../lib/seo/meta';
import { articleSchema, breadcrumbSchema, graph, organizationSchema } from '../lib/seo/schema';
import { SITE } from '../lib/config/site';

const UPDATED = '2026-09-24';
const site = Astro.site ?? Astro.url;
const title = 'Spiti road guide: Shimla, Kinnaur, Kaza, Kunzum & Manali';
const description =
  'How the Spiti circuit works by road: the Kinnaur route from Shimla, Kaza and its villages, the seasonal Kunzum to Chandratal to Manali side, when to go and what it means for your vehicle.';
const meta = buildPageMeta({
  title,
  description,
  path: '/spiti-road-guide/',
  site,
  ogType: 'article',
});
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Spiti road guide', path: '/spiti-road-guide/' },
];
const jsonLd = graph(
  organizationSchema(site),
  articleSchema({ headline: title, description, url: meta.canonical, dateModified: UPDATED, site }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, site),
);
const route = 'Shimla → Spiti → Manali';
---

<PageLayout
  meta={meta}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  eyebrow="Spiti road guide"
  title="The road to Spiti,"
  titleAccent="section by section."
  intro="What each part of the Shimla → Kinnaur → Kaza → Manali circuit is like by road, and what changes with the season."
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <WhatsAppLink slot="hero-actions" class="button button-whatsapp" cta="page" routeLabel={route}>
    Check the road for my dates ↗
  </WhatsAppLink>
  <article class="shell prose guide">
    <p class="guide-updated">
      Updated{' '}
      {new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-IN', {
        day: 'numeric',
        month: 'long',
        year: 'numeric',
        timeZone: 'UTC',
      }).format(new Date(UPDATED))}
      . Road and weather conditions change; we confirm them for your dates.
    </p>

    <h2>Two ways in, one circuit</h2>
    <p>
      Spiti can be reached from Shimla through Kinnaur, or from Manali over Kunzum Pass. Our{' '}
      <a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/">9 day private circuit</a> goes in through Kinnaur and comes
      out via Kunzum, Chandratal and Manali. Going in from the Shimla side gains height gradually,
      which gives your body time to adjust before the high villages around Kaza.
    </p>

    <h2>Shimla to Kinnaur</h2>
    <p>
      The road follows the Sutlej valley on NH 5 through Narkanda and Rampur to Karcham, where the
      Baspa river joins the Sutlej. From there a side road climbs into the Sangla valley, with
      Rakcham and Chitkul further up (<a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day1">day 1</a> and{' '}
      <a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day2">day 2</a>). Reckong Peo is Kinnaur's main town; Kalpa
      sits above it with wide mountain views.
    </p>
    <p>
      Beyond Pooh the valley narrows and the road is cut into the cliffs, with landslide prone and
      under repair stretches. It is driven in daylight and at an unhurried pace. Nako, and the stop
      at Gue, lead to Tabo on the Spiti side (<a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day3">day 3</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>Tabo, Kaza and the high villages</h2>
    <p>
      Tabo's old monastery, Dhankar on its ridge and the optional Pin Valley detour lead to Kaza,
      the main town of Spiti and the base for local days (
      <a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day4">day 4</a>). From Kaza, short drives reach Key
      Monastery, Kibber and Chicham Bridge (<a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day5">day 5</a>), and
      the villages of Langza, Hikkim and Komic (<a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day6">day 6</a>).
      A slow day in Kaza (<a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day7">day 7</a>) helps with altitude and
      gives a weather buffer.
    </p>

    <h2>Kunzum Pass and Chandratal (seasonal)</h2>
    <p>
      West of Kaza the road passes Losar and climbs over Kunzum Pass, at around 4,550 m. A side road
      beyond the pass leads to Chandratal lake (<a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day8">day 8</a>).
      This section is usually open only in the warmer months, roughly from early summer to autumn,
      and closes with snow. Camps near the lake are seasonal too.
    </p>

    <h2>Batal to Manali</h2>
    <p>
      From Chandratal the road runs through Batal to Gramphu, a rough stretch with stream crossings
      whose water level changes through the day. At Gramphu it joins the Manali road, and the Atal
      Tunnel leads down to the Manali side (<a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/#day9">day 9</a>). When
      Kunzum is closed, the return goes back through Kinnaur instead.
    </p>

    <h2>When to go</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Full circuit via Kunzum and Chandratal:</strong> only while the pass is open,
        usually summer to early autumn.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Kinnaur route to Kaza:</strong> used through most of the year, but snow, landslides
        and road work can still cause closures.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Monsoon months:</strong> the Kinnaur side can see landslides; build in buffer time.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We check the current status of each section before confirming a trip.</p>

    <h2>What it means for your vehicle</h2>
    <p>
      We travel in an <a href="/vehicles/innova-crysta/">Innova Crysta</a>: comfortable on the long
      Kinnaur drive with room for luggage. It is not a 4×4 snow expedition vehicle, so high pass and
      stream crossing sections are confirmed trip by trip for the conditions at the time.
    </p>

    <h2>Before you travel</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Altitude:</strong> take it slow, drink water and keep the rest day. Tell us if
        anyone has health concerns.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Permits:</strong> foreign nationals need a permit for the border stretch between
        Kinnaur and Spiti. Check the current rules before you travel.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Connectivity and cash:</strong> mobile network is patchy beyond the main towns and
        ATMs are few, so carry some cash.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Official updates:</strong> see the{' '}
        <a href={SITE.officialRouteGuidance.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          {SITE.officialRouteGuidance.label}
        </a>
        .
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="guide-cta">
      <h2>Plan the drive for your dates</h2>
      <p>
        Send your dates and group size. We confirm which sections are open and suggest the route.
      </p>
      <WhatsAppLink class="button button-whatsapp" cta="page" routeLabel={route}>
        Start WhatsApp conversation ↗
      </WhatsAppLink>
      <p>
        <a href="/routes/shimla-to-spiti/">See the full 9 day itinerary →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
